# How to work in this repo (agents)

Follow this loop for any implementation task in __PROJECT_NAME__.

## Before writing code
1. Read `docs/README.md` and open only the files it maps to your task.
2. Read `docs/02-constraints/invariants.md` — always.
3. Search `docs/03-decisions/` for ADRs tagged for your area. Respect accepted
   ones.
4. If you work on a version, read `docs/plans/vX.Y.Z.T/architecture.md` and
   `plan.md` (your goal's Outcome and Definition of Done), and the feature
   tests the goal covers.

## If your task involves a new architectural decision
(new dependency, new pattern, new service, changed boundary)
- Draft an ADR as `Proposed` using `03-decisions/_template.md` BEFORE implementing.
- Get it confirmed to `Accepted`, then build to it.

## If implementation would break an invariant or an accepted ADR
- Stop. Raise it with the user, or propose a superseding ADR.
- Do NOT quietly work around the rule or rewrite it to match your code.

## While implementing
- Match `04-conventions/`.
- Keep changes scoped to the task.

## After finishing
- Commit with Conventional Commits (`04-conventions/git-workflow.md`).
- Update affected docs: architecture/component descriptions
  (`engineer:sync-docs` does this for a version).
- Run the PR checklist in `04-conventions/git-workflow.md`.

## Direction of truth
Description docs (architecture, components, data-model) follow the code.
Constraints and ADRs lead the code. Never edit an invariant just to make a
failing check pass.
